#!/usr/bin/env node
// Host-conformance fixture: verifier writes a schema-valid `allow` verdict to
// STDERR and nothing at all to stdout, then exits 0. §5.3 says hosts MUST NOT
// parse stderr for the verdict; §5.2 says empty stdout is a fail-closed
// condition. A conforming host MUST deny with failure_class
// unparseable_stdout rather than 'helpfully' falling back to stderr. Offered
// case (1): malformed (empty) stdout.
